pages.body:
for each `r`, it counts the decisions across all landmark counts, leaving out empty cells, and returns:
- the probability of rejecting and of accepting;
- the [[ambiguity]], 4 · p(accept) · p(reject).

these are the numbers drawn in the [[decision_landscape]].

it iterates the [[intrinsic_mean]] update on gr(d, n_re):
- log-map every shape at the current estimate;
- average the tangent vectors;
- exp-map the average back.

it stops when the size of the update ‖v‖ falls below tolerance. the ‖v‖ history is printed and kept, so convergence can be checked rather than assumed.

the result `x0` is the centre every later distance and mode is measured from.

a two-sample test only makes sense if both ensembles are described in the **same** coordinates. this routine:

- runs [[srqd]] on the two ensembles with one shared [[reference_shape]], which may be given as a function of the landmark count, such as [[chiral_reference]];
- computes one intrinsic mean and one set of pga modes from the pooled shapes, on both the grassmannian and spd;
- expresses every shape of both ensembles in that shared basis.

it is called once per landmark count by [[shapemmd]] and [[gmmd|shape_gmmd]]. with [[cut]] on, shapes beyond the convexity radius are removed from the **pooled** set first, so either ensemble can come back smaller than it went in.
